# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# koris-hub — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local work. Next.js loads `.env` and `.env.local`
# (both git-ignored); nothing here reaches the browser unless it is prefixed
# with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# The Cloudflare Worker does NOT read this file — it loads `worker/.dev.vars`
# (next to worker/wrangler.toml) in dev, and Worker secrets in production.
# See worker/.dev.vars.example.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Build-time (optional) -------------------------------------------------
# Personal access token used by the force-static /api/changelog and
# /api/downloads routes when they call the GitHub Releases API during
# `next build` (src/lib/github-releases.ts). Without it those calls are
# unauthenticated and share GitHub's low per-IP rate limit, which can make the
# build's changelog/downloads data empty. No scopes are needed for public repos.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Cloudflare Worker deploy (manual) -------------------------------------
# Credentials for `pnpm worker:deploy`. Not needed for `pnpm worker:dev` or for
# building/deploying the site itself. Create a token at
# https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens with the "Edit Cloudflare
# Workers" permission plus access to the koaris.com zone.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# --- Cloudflare Worker runtime secrets (documentation only) ----------------
# Set the Jev key once in production instead of putting it here:
#     cd worker && pnpm dlx wrangler secret put TYPESAFE_API_KEY
# For local Worker development, put it in worker/.dev.vars.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# TYPESAFE_API_BASE=https://api.typesafe.ai
